  "description": "LIV-143 Havenreach town (`town_havenreach`) NPC roster — unique 3D models only, no tinting. The board (rejected confirmation on LIV-141) directed that NPC variety must come from the source 3D models themselves, not colour tints used to stretch a small mesh set into a bigger cast. The town therefore ships exactly one NPC per unique rigged human GLB: `villager_m`, `deckhand_walk`, `first_fisher`, `villager_f`, `young_fisher`, `child_white_hair` (six models -> six NPCs). The three primary quest givers (Captain Halden, Wick, The Weigher) stay stationary in front of the three structures at the top of the town; the three remaining cast members are ambient wanderers spread across the districts. Every sprite is a genuine render of its own model in the model's own colours — `renderTheme` tint fallbacks are removed, and no NPC is a recolour of another. Each NPC still declares `npcSpriteId > spriteId > type` resolve order; `spriteId`, `svgCode` and `portraitEmoji` stay as the harmless migration fallbacks (they are only used if an authored asset is ever missing). `aiType` remains the neutral-entity dispatch key (stationary|wander). Quest wiring is unchanged: `quests.json` `giverNpcId`/`turnInNpcId` resolve, and every retained NPC's dialogue id resolves in `dialogues.json`. LIV-145 adds an optional per-NPC `renderScale` (`{ w, h }` multiplier, default 1) applied to the LIV-142 humanoid render box so a short/tall character reads correctly while staying centre-bottom anchored (shadow + HP/quest-marker anchors track the scaled box).",
